    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_pdp_171'), 'A volume check compared tonight''s row count with yesterday''s:

```text
business day   orders
2026-11-01     20,104
2026-11-02     21,870
...
2026-11-07     40,315   (11.11 promotion)
2026-11-08     20,880   -> volume check FAILED: 52% of yesterday
```

Statement: "Comparing with the median of the previous 7 business days instead of with yesterday keeps this alert from firing: one promotion day does not move the median."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. The median of the 7 previous days is about 20,500, and 20,880 is a normal night; only the comparison with the promotion day made it look like a 48% drop. A median (or same weekday in recent weeks) is robust to one unusual day, so the check fires on real drops and not after every campaign. The misconception is that the most recent day is the best baseline; it is the most volatile one.', 3, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_pdp_171') AND order_index = 3)
